+`judged_text` sets what the judge reads as the completion: `reply` (the default),
+`thinking_and_reply`, or `conversation`, which puts the question in front of those. Thinking comes
+from the response's reasoning items, so a model without them is judged on its reply in every view.
+
 A judge failure says nothing about the response, so NeMo-RL leaves a flagged sample out of the
 loss. A reply that gives no digit is a failure too, and so is a prompt over the judge's context.
 Per-rubric scores come back as `rubric_<name>` fields.
